 The adapter formerly made `demos` and `queries` keyword-only, which rejected the native worker's four-positional-argument interface with `TypeError: generate() takes 2 positional arguments but 4 were given`. The current adapter accepts positional demo/query counts and retains keyword-only `max_attempts`; no prototype rule, generator, typed-grid check, or teaching assertion changed. Current adapter SHA-256 is `34656cfa470a0d8a83a7c493f5f2d3eddeb54bf929fe800440359e24f399d1c8`. The existing real-Racket adapter regression now exercises positional counts, failed before this repair, and all 28 focused prototype tests pass afterward. The source-bound reproduction and focused receipt are in `workspace/parametric/evidence/owner-native-adapter/`; the native inventory includes retained external reviewer evidence separately.
 
 Native qualification and owner acceptance now pass on all three settings at seeds 0 and 17 with three demonstrations and four queries: six episodes per gate, 78 protected Racket evaluations in qualification and 78 in fresh acceptance replay. `parametric/accepted.json` binds the current source closure and task-owned execution evidence; native status is `accepted` with `training_admitted: false`. Retained external checks remain reviewer-reported. This bounded check establishes neither universal identifiability nor measured training benefit, and does not change the canonical generator or downstream training admission.
+
+## Open peer finding: border-only rotation survives the demonstrations
+
+On generator SHA-256 `ff975d4d5cce91725c18577964ebebef03a1b543ed6a9f4bcb68f9a11c4dc802` and prototype SHA-256 `1271276c1c0c3a36ca3fad89f0bff96fb6a5c9a903fefd6e5af128e35b65350a`, the retained native default episode at seed 0 (`quarter_turns=2`, three demonstrations) admits the plausible wrong rule “rotate the outer border by 180 degrees and leave the interior unchanged.” All three 3×3 demonstrations fit this rival exactly: the only interior cell is the fixed center. The first 4×5 query disagrees with the canonical rule at all six interior cells. Fresh generation reproduced sample indices 0–3 exactly, and eight actual protected-Racket evaluations confirmed both programs on those four inputs.
+
+Runnable reproducer: `workspace/border_rotation_probe.py`. Source-bound inputs, both programs, outputs and protected runtime identity are in the current reviewer return at `WORK/checks/88b8e6aaa49d/border_rotation.json`; its successful command receipt is `border_rotation.command.json` in the same directory. This is one seed, one named rival and the first query only. The existing D4 and declared quarter-turn checks do not include this rival.
+
+Recommended next repair: replace one existing demonstration with an interior-distinguishing rectangular or larger-square example before the first larger query, keeping the demonstration count, and explicitly refute the border-only rival. That requires revisiting the fixed three-palette demonstration schedule; the present peer review retains the witness without changing selected generator or accepted prototype source. The finding remains open.
